<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<chapter xml:id="ch-vectors" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Vectors in <m>\R^n</m></title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      The columns of an augmented matrix are more than bookkeeping. Treating them as
      vectors turns a system of equations into a question about linear combinations:
      can a given vector be built out of a given collection of others? The vocabulary of
      span and linear independence, developed here, is what the rest of the book is
      written in.
    </p>
  </introduction>

  <xi:include href="vectors/sec-vectors-in-rn.ptx" />
